class:: TGeometricRand
summary:: Triggered geometric failures-before-success sampler
categories:: UGens>Generators>Stochastic>Distributions
related:: Guides/StochasticDynamicsUGens, Classes/TPoissonRand, Classes/TIRand

description::

Returns the number of failures before the first success using an inverse logarithmic transform. Probability at or above one returns zero; probability at or below zero returns the largest exactly representable integer float.

Like link::Classes/TIRand::, it returns discrete triggered values; unlike TIRand, its support begins at zero and follows a geometric tail.

subsection:: Probability mass

image::geometric-mass.png#Failures-before-success mass functions for probability = 0.2, 0.5, and 0.8, shown in muted teal, blue, and plum. A smaller success probability produces the longer discrete tail.::

classmethods::

method:: ar
argument:: probability
Success probability in code::(0, 1):: with explicit endpoint fallbacks.
argument:: trig
Resample on a rising edge.
argument:: seed
Init-rate local seed.
argument:: reset
Restore the seed and sample a new initial value.
argument:: mul
Output multiplier.
argument:: add
Output offset.

method:: kr
Control-rate version with the same arguments.

instancemethods::

examples::

code::
(
{ TGeometricRand.kr(0.3, Impulse.kr(5)).poll }.play
)
::

code::
(
{ SinOsc.ar((TGeometricRand.kr(0.35, Impulse.kr(8)) + 1) * 140, 0, 0.08) }.play
)
::

